I draw my dagger and charge the wounded orc. He catches my approach and swings his heavy mace in a vicious horizontal arc aimed at my jaw.

Time slows. I duck beneath the whistling iron and thrust my dagger upward into his exposed heart before he can recover his balance. The mace slips from limp fingers, clattering against the stones as he drops.

A second orc charges instantly, his mace raised overhead.
}
